    <briefdescription>
<para>Axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) for a contiguous block of curve points, used for hit-test culling. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The AABB is stored in data-space so it never needs rebuilding during pan/zoom — only when the underlying data changes. It intentionally extends one point beyond each chunk boundary so that line segments bridging adjacent chunks are always covered. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
